# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log
logs/
!logs/.gitkeep

# Deck presets — snapshots of whatever cards a wizard happened to be carrying,
# personal to one account and not meaningful to anyone else.  strategies/duel/
# and strategies/player/ stay tracked: those are shareable strategy definitions.
# Deck data embedded in a bot_strategies/ file is also tracked — it is part of
# what makes that specific strategy runnable.
# The directory is recreated on demand (list_deck_presets tolerates it missing).
strategies/decks/

# Real player data — see CLAUDE.md, "No real player data".
#
# Some tools record actual character names and ids by design, and those must never be
# committed: this repo is public, and a real wizard name links the account to whoever wrote
# the commit. The tools write to these paths specifically so an accidental commit is not
# possible by mistake.
#
# tools/name_key_samples.json is NOT ignored and stays tracked — it is the synthetic
# fixture, built from the shipped name tables, that `name_keys.py --verify` checks against.
# `probe_name_behavior.py --record` writes the .local.json beside it instead.
#
# The infix is what carries the meaning, not the extension: drop exports land as
# .local.csv, and `probe_chat_log_size.py --csv` writes one too, refusing any other
# suffix so a recording cannot land on a tracked path. Anything else that records live
# account data should follow the same naming rather than needing a new rule here.
*.local.*
probe_*_report.txt

# Claude
# Personal Claude state stays out of the repo; project skills are shared
# tooling and are tracked. A bare `.claude/` would stop git descending at
# all, so the negation needs the glob form.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
